  "body": "The [textarea](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-textarea-element) component seems to be implemented across browsers with a mechanism in the lower right corner for pointer users to expand/resize the component. However, the component lacks a documented keyboard equivalent for this, thus failing [WCAG 2.1.1](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/Understanding/keyboard.html)\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/14298245/199058750-1b4fade2-afb0-4daa-8272-4e0890d7c9f9.png)\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/14298245/199059229-f6dc72dc-ec1b-4097-a0f4-91480758a74d.png)\r\n\r\nWhile I realize this could be considered a user agent issue, given the global implementation and usefulness of the resize mechanism, I'm wondering if HTML5 has any ability to document this optional behaviour and potentially suggest accessibility considerations, such as putting the mechanism in the tab order or surfacing a keyboard shortcut on focus.\r\n\r\n",
